/* ============================================================================
   GOD SQUAD — component-facets.css
   Phase 13. Shopify's native filtering, in one element.

   THE SAME MARKUP IS TWO LAYOUTS.

   snippets/facets.liquid emits the filter controls exactly once. Above --bp-md
   they are a horizontal row of dropdowns; below it, once script has upgraded
   them, the same element is a drawer. Nothing is duplicated, so there is one
   checked state and nothing to keep in step.

   THE DRAWER IS OPT-IN, NOT THE BASE STATE.

   position:fixed is applied only under .facets--drawer, a class assets/facets.js
   adds. That ordering is load-bearing: with no script the panel has to be IN
   FLOW and visible, because the button that would open a drawer is the thing
   script was going to reveal. A fixed panel with no opener is a filter UI a
   customer cannot reach.

   So the base state — a stack of collapsed groups above the grid — is the
   no-script state, and it is already a usable mobile filter UI.
   ========================================================================== */

.facets {
  margin-block-end: var(--space-5);
}

/* The drawer's own title row. Below --bp-md it is the drawer header; above it
   there is no layer, so it is not needed. */
.facets__bar {
  display: none;
}

.facets__groups {
  display: grid;
  gap: var(--space-2);
}

/* -------------------------------------------------------------- one group */

.facets__group {
  border-block-end: var(--border-width) solid var(--color-border-current-subtle);
}

/* The whole disclosure is <details>/<summary>. No ARIA, no script: the same
   reasoning sections/main-product.liquid records for its description. */
.facets__summary {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--space-2);
  /* --target-min tall. A filter group heading is a primary control on this
     surface, and Phase 9 set the floor. */
  min-height: var(--target-min);
  padding-block: var(--space-3);
  cursor: pointer;
  color: inherit;
  font-family: var(--font-body);
  font-size: var(--type-label-size);
  font-weight: var(--type-label-weight);
  letter-spacing: var(--type-label-ls);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  list-style: none;
}

/* Safari still paints its own disclosure triangle without this. */
.facets__summary::-webkit-details-marker {
  display: none;
}

.facets__summary-label {
  flex: 1 1 auto;
}

/* The applied count, so a collapsed group still says it is doing something. */
.facets__summary-count {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  min-width: 1.5rem;
  height: 1.5rem;
  padding-inline: var(--space-2);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background-color: var(--accent-current);
  color: var(--color-bg-primary);
  font-size: var(--type-caption-size);
}

.surface-light .facets__summary-count {
  color: var(--color-bg-secondary);
}

/* Phase 18. The base rotation was missing, so this pointed RIGHT closed and
   LEFT open — a 180° flip with nothing to flip from. icon-chevron.svg is drawn
   pointing right (see the snippet), so a disclosure has to turn it down before
   the open state means anything.

   PHASE-2-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md §18 line 1489 permits exactly one transform, "the
   chevron rotating 180° when its disclosure opens", and line 2917 describes one
   mark "rotated in CSS for all four directions" — the 180° was implemented, the
   direction it rotates FROM was not. 90deg to -90deg is still 180°, and it is
   what sections/main-product.liquid's disclosure already does, so all three
   disclosures now agree: down at rest, up when open.

   Size is deliberately left alone. Line 1428 assigns the chevron "--icon-sm
   16px inline; --icon-md in controls", so 16px in a compact filter row and 24px
   on the product accordion are both the specified value, not drift. */
.facets__summary .icon {
  flex: 0 0 auto;
  width: var(--icon-sm);
  height: var(--icon-sm);
  transform: rotate(90deg);
  transition: transform var(--transition-fast);
}

.facets__group[open] .facets__summary .icon {
  transform: rotate(-90deg);
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------- the values */

.facets__values {
  padding-block-end: var(--space-4);
}

.facets__list {
  display: grid;
  gap: var(--space-1);
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
}

.facets__value {
  position: relative;
}

/* The checkbox carries the theme's shared .visually-hidden utility rather than
   re-declaring the same six properties here — the pattern
   snippets/product-variant-picker.liquid established for its radios. It stays
   in the document and focusable; the ring is drawn on the label it controls,
   and the label is the 44px target. */

.facets__label {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--space-3);
  /* 44px, not the 24px AA floor: a filter value is a primary control on this
     surface and there is no larger equivalent beside it. */
  min-height: var(--target-min);
  padding-inline: var(--space-2);
  cursor: pointer;
  color: var(--color-text-current-muted);
  font-family: var(--font-body);
  font-size: var(--type-body-sm-size);
  line-height: var(--type-body-sm-lh);
}

/* The box is drawn, not native, so its border can use the interactive token
   that measures 3:1 — Phase 2 §12.2. Native checkbox accent colours cannot be
   measured against the surface they land on. */
.facets__label::before {
  content: '';
  flex: 0 0 auto;
  width: 1rem;
  height: 1rem;
  border: var(--border-width) solid var(--color-border-current-interactive);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background-color: transparent;
}

.facets__checkbox:checked + .facets__label {
  color: inherit;
}

.facets__checkbox:checked + .facets__label::before {
  border-color: var(--accent-current);
  background-color: var(--accent-current);
}

.facets__checkbox:focus-visible + .facets__label {
  outline: var(--focus-width) solid var(--focus-ring);
  outline-offset: var(--focus-offset);
}

.facets__label-text {
  flex: 1 1 auto;
}

/* Shopify's own count. Muted, because it is a hint rather than a value. */
.facets__count {
  flex: 0 0 auto;
  color: var(--color-text-current-muted);
  font-size: var(--type-caption-size);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

/* A swatch is decorative — the colour's NAME is beside it, so the mark is never
   the only carrier (SC 1.4.1). The border keeps a cream swatch visible on a
   cream surface. */
.facets__swatch {
  flex: 0 0 auto;
  width: var(--swatch-size);
  height: var(--swatch-size);
  border: var(--border-width) solid var(--color-border-current);
  border-radius: 50%;
  background-color: var(--facet-swatch, transparent);
}

/* --------------------------------------------------------------- price */

.facets__price {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  gap: var(--space-3);
  padding-inline: var(--space-2);
}

.facets__price-field label {
  display: block;
  margin-block-end: var(--space-2);
  color: var(--color-text-current-muted);
  font-family: var(--font-body);
  font-size: var(--type-caption-size);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: var(--type-caption-ls);
}

.facets__price-input {
  width: 100%;
  min-height: var(--control-height);
  padding-inline: var(--space-3);
  border: var(--border-width) solid var(--color-border-current-interactive);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background-color: transparent;
  color: inherit;
  font-family: var(--font-body);
  /* 16px: below it iOS zooms the viewport on focus. */
  font-size: var(--type-body-size);
}

/* --------------------------------------------------------------- footer
   Apply and Clear all. Only a drawer needs them: above --bp-md the toolbar's
   own submit does the applying and the chips do the clearing. */

.facets__footer {
  display: none;
  gap: var(--space-3);
  padding-block-start: var(--space-4);
}

.facets__clear,
.facets-active__clear {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  min-height: var(--target-min);
  color: var(--color-text-current-muted);
  font-family: var(--font-body);
  font-size: var(--type-body-sm-size);
  text-decoration: underline;
  text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------- applied filters
   Chips are links carrying Shopify's own url_to_remove. Small and quiet: the
   brief asks for them to be easy to remove and NOT visually dominant, so they
   are outlined rather than filled and sit at the caption size. */

.facets-active {
  margin-block-end: var(--space-5);
}

.facets-active__list {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
}

.facets-active__chip {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--space-2);
  /* 24px is the SC 2.5.8 floor. A chip is a secondary control and its removal
     is also reachable from the group it came from, which is the equivalent
     control that exception allows. */
  min-height: var(--target-min-aa);
  padding: var(--space-1) var(--space-3);
  border: var(--border-width) solid var(--color-border-current);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  color: inherit;
  font-family: var(--font-body);
  font-size: var(--type-caption-size);
  letter-spacing: var(--type-caption-ls);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  text-decoration: none;
}

.facets-active__group {
  color: var(--color-text-current-muted);
}

/* --icon-sm is the smallest the scale defines. A chip's close mark is the one
   place that wants smaller still, so it is scaled from the token rather than
   given a magic number of its own. */
.facets-active__chip .icon {
  width: calc(var(--icon-sm) * 0.75);
  height: calc(var(--icon-sm) * 0.75);
}

@media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) {
  .facets-active__chip:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent-current);
  }
}

/* ============================================================== the drawer
   Below --bp-md, and ONLY once assets/facets.js has added .facets--drawer.
   ========================================================================== */

@media (max-width: 767px) {
  .facets--drawer {
    position: fixed;
    inset-block: 0;
    inset-inline-end: 0;
    z-index: var(--z-drawer);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    width: var(--drawer-width);
    max-width: 100%;
    margin-block-end: 0;
    padding: var(--space-5);
    background-color: var(--color-bg-primary);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-on-dark);
    transform: translateX(100%);
    transition: transform var(--transition-medium);
    visibility: hidden;
  }

  .facets--drawer.is-open {
    transform: translateX(0);
    visibility: visible;
  }

  /* Phase 18. The exit slide was never seen: `visibility` is not a transitioned
     property here, so removing .is-open flipped it to hidden in the same frame
     the transform started and the panel vanished instead of sliding out.
     PHASE-2 §21 line 1725 assigns "menu panel / drawer entry AND exit" the
     medium duration, so the exit is specified, not decoration.

     assets/facets.js adds this class on close and removes it on transitionend,
     with a timeout fallback — the same shape assets/cart.js uses for the cart
     drawer, which is the one other drawer in the theme and already animates its
     exit correctly. Doing it in JS rather than with a `visibility 0s linear
     250ms` delay keeps the two drawers on one pattern. */
  .facets--drawer.is-closing {
    visibility: visible;
  }

  .facets--drawer .facets__bar {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    padding-block-end: var(--space-4);
    border-block-end: var(--border-width) solid var(--color-border-current);
  }

  /* The groups scroll, the header and footer do not — so Apply is always
     reachable however many filters a merchant has configured. */
  .facets--drawer .facets__groups {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    overflow-y: auto;
    overscroll-behavior: contain;
    padding-block: var(--space-4);
  }

  .facets--drawer .facets__footer {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    justify-items: center;
  }

  /* The phone's home indicator sits under the footer, and Apply is in it. */
  @supports (padding: max(0px)) {
    .facets--drawer {
      padding-block-end: max(var(--space-5), env(safe-area-inset-bottom));
    }
  }
}

/* Phase 18: --font-body, not --font-display. design-tokens.css:170 states the
   rule — "Playfair for H1-H2, Jost for H3-H4 (interface headings)" — and
   PHASE-2 §6.1 assigns the h3/h4 rows the body family at weight 600. It also
   made the weight honest: the display font is registered as playfair_display_n9
   with no font_modify, so --weight-semibold against a 900-only family resolved
   to 900. Jost 600 IS registered (layout/theme.liquid), so 600 now means 600. */
.facets__bar-title {
  margin: 0;
  font-family: var(--font-body);
  font-size: var(--type-h4-size);
  font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
}

.facets__close {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  min-width: var(--target-min);
  min-height: var(--target-min);
  border: 0;
  background: none;
  color: inherit;
  cursor: pointer;
}

/* ------------------------------------------------- the horizontal bar
   --bp-md and up. A row of dropdowns above the toolbar. An open group overlays
   the grid rather than reflowing it, which is what keeps the bar's cost a
   one-time 72px rather than a jump every time a customer opens a group. */

@media (min-width: 768px) {
  .facets__groups {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-5);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .facets__group {
    position: relative;
    border-block-end: 0;
  }

  .facets__values {
    position: absolute;
    inset-block-start: 100%;
    inset-inline-start: 0;
    z-index: var(--z-raised);
    min-width: 14rem;
    padding: var(--space-4);
    border: var(--border-width) solid var(--color-border-current);
    background-color: var(--color-bg-primary);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-elevated);
  }

  .surface-light .facets__values {
    background-color: var(--color-bg-secondary);
  }

  .facets__price {
    min-width: 18rem;
  }
}

/* ============================================================== page state
   The lock is a class on <html>, matching the header's menu panel and NOT
   assets/cart.js's inline fixed-position lock. Two class-based owners compose:
   each adds and removes its own class, and overflow:hidden is still in force
   while either is present. Two inline-style owners would fight over one
   recorded scroll position.
   ========================================================================== */

.facets-open body {
  overflow: hidden;
}

/* [hidden] loses to the .button class at equal specificity — the same defect
   Phase 11 found on the header panel — so the trigger needs this to stay
   hidden until assets/facets.js reveals it. */
.main-collection__filter-toggle[hidden] {
  display: none;
}

/* ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING HERE, AND IT WAS WRONG.

   The base rule must come FIRST and the media query second. A media query adds
   no specificity, so when the unconditional `display: inline-flex` sat AFTER
   the `@media (min-width: 768px) { display: none }` block, both selectors were
   (0,1,0) and the later one won at every width. The retirement rule had never
   once applied.

   That is not cosmetic. This rule is the no-script half of the Phase 16 P0 fix:
   with scripting off, facets.js never runs, never sets the hidden attribute,
   and this media query is the only thing standing between a desktop keyboard
   user and a focusable Filter button that opens nothing — SC 2.1.2, the exact
   trap Phase 16 closed for the scripted case. Phase 18's audit reported the
   dead rule as a LOW cosmetic finding; it is the accessibility guard.

   Caught by running the suite under Chrome after Edge's --dump-dom broke: the
   trigger measured display:flex at 1280 where 1440 and 768 both hid it.

   display:none rather than visibility or opacity, because it must also leave
   the tab order — a focusable control that opens nothing is worse than one that
   is merely invisible. header.css retires the mobile menu button the same way. */
.main-collection__filter-toggle {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--space-2);
}

/* Retired above --bp-md, where there is no drawer for it to open. */
@media (min-width: 768px) {
  .main-collection__filter-toggle {
    display: none;
  }
}

.main-collection__filter-count {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  min-width: 1.25rem;
  height: 1.25rem;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  background-color: var(--accent-current);
  color: var(--color-bg-primary);
  font-size: var(--type-caption-size);
}

/* The editor-only note, when a merchant has switched filters on but has not
   created any in the admin app yet. */
.main-collection__notice {
  margin: 0 0 var(--space-5);
  padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
  border-inline-start: var(--border-width-strong) solid var(--accent-current);
  color: var(--color-text-current-muted);
  font-family: var(--font-body);
  font-size: var(--type-body-sm-size);
  line-height: var(--type-body-sm-lh);
}
